// Period selector for Solution C.
//
// A parameter model: a one-row query whose only job is to carry a
// dashboard dropdown value into AQL. Nothing joins to it.
//
// This exists because the two things are different in Holistics:
//
//   - A FIELD filter (Fiscal Year, Fiscal Quarter) filters the query
//     automatically. Every block on the page obeys it, including blocks
//     added later, and nothing has to reference it.
//   - A PARAM filter carries a value into AQL. Only metrics that
//     explicitly read it are affected.
//
// A single-select "Period" dropdown has to be a param, because the
// windows overlap - every QTD date is also a YTD date, and every YTD
// date is also in this fiscal year - and one field can only hold one
// value per row. So the choice lives here and `gmv_period` in the
// dataset reads it.
//
// The five values pair up. "This fiscal year" / "This fiscal quarter"
// are the whole period; "Fiscal YTD" / "Fiscal QTD" stop at today. On a
// warehouse whose data ends today the two halves of a pair return the
// same number - the difference only shows where rows are dated in the
// future, which is exactly Seed's HubSpot close-date pipeline case.
//
// The cost of that choice: a new chart written against plain `gmv`
// will silently ignore this dropdown. Point new charts at `gmv_period`.
Model seed_c_period {
  type: 'query'
  label: 'Period Selector'
  description: 'Parameter model carrying the Period dropdown (Full history / This fiscal year / Fiscal YTD / This fiscal quarter / Fiscal QTD) into AQL. Not joined to anything.'
  data_source_name: 'demodb'
  query: @sql select 1 as dummy ;;
  models: [
  ]

  param window {
    label: 'Period'
    type: 'text'
    allowed_values: [
      'Full history',
      'This fiscal year',
      'Fiscal YTD',
      'This fiscal quarter',
      'Fiscal QTD'
    ]
  }
}
